# AWS Well-Architected Framework Framework

> The AWS Well-Architected Framework helps you understand the pros and cons of decisions you make while building systems on AWS. By using the Framework you will learn architectural best practices for designing and operating reliable, secure, efficient, cost-effective, and sustainable systems in the cloud.

- [The review process](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/the-review-process.md)
- [Conclusion](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/conclusion.md)
- [Contributors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/contributors.md)
- [Further reading](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/further-reading.md)
- [Document revisions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/document-revisions.md)
- [Notices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/notices.md)
- [AWS Glossary](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/glossary.md)

## [Abstract and introduction](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/welcome.md)

- [Definitions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/definitions.md): Definitions
- [On architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/on-architecture.md): In on-premises environments, customers often have a central team for technology architecture that acts as an overlay to other product or feature teams to verify they are following best practice.
- [General design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/general-design-principles.md): The Well-Architected Framework identifies a set of general design principles to facilitate good design in the cloud.


## [The pillars of the framework](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/the-pillars-of-the-framework.md)

### [Operational excellence](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/operational-excellence.md)

Operational excellence (OE) is a commitment to build software correctly while consistently delivering a great customer experience.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-design-principles.md): There are five design principles for operational excellence in the cloud.
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-definition.md): There are four best practice areas for operational excellence in the cloud: organization, prepare, operate, and evolve.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-organization.md): Your teams must have a shared understanding of your entire workload, their role in it, and shared business goals to set the priorities that will achieve business success.
- [Prepare](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-prepare.md): To prepare for operational excellence, you have to understand your workloads and their expected behaviors.
- [Operate](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-operate.md): Successful operation of a workload is measured by the achievement of business and customer outcomes.
- [Evolve](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-evolve.md): Learn, share, and continuously improve to sustain operational excellence.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/oe-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for Operational Excellence.

### [Security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/security.md)

The Security pillar encompasses the ability to protect data, systems, and assets to take advantage of cloud technologies to improve your security.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-design.md): In the cloud, there are a number of principles that can help you strengthen your workload security.
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-def.md): There are seven best practice areas for security in the cloud.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Security foundations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-security.md): To operate your workload securely, you must apply overarching best practices to every area of security.
- [Identity and access management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-iam.md): Identity and access management are key parts of an information security program, ensuring that only authorized and authenticated users and components are able to access your resources, and only in a manner that you intend.
- [Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-detection.md): You can use detective controls to identify a potential security threat or incident.
- [Infrastructure protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-infrastructure.md): Infrastructure protection encompasses control methodologies, such as defense in depth, necessary to meet best practices and organizational or regulatory obligations.
- [Data protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-dataprot.md): Before architecting any system, foundational practices that influence security should be in place.
- [Incident response](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-incresp.md): Even with extremely mature preventive and detective controls, your organization should still put processes in place to respond to and mitigate the potential impact of security incidents.
- [Application security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-appsec.md): Application security (AppSec) describes the overall process of how you design, build, and test the security properties of the workloads you develop.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for Security.

### [Reliability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/reliability.md)

The Reliability pillar encompasses the ability of a workload to perform its intended function correctly and consistently when it’s expected to.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-dp.md): There are five design principles for reliability in the cloud.
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-def.md): There are four best practice areas for reliability in the cloud: foundations, workload architecture, change management, and failure management.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Foundations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-found.md): Foundational requirements are those whose scope extends beyond a single workload or project.
- [Workload architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-workload-arch.md): A reliable workload starts with upfront design decisions for both software and infrastructure.
- [Change management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-chg-mgmt.md): Changes to your workload or its environment must be anticipated and accommodated to achieve reliable operation of the workload.
- [Failure management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-failmgmt.md): In any system of reasonable complexity, it is expected that failures will occur.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for Reliability.

### [Performance efficiency](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/performance-efficiency.md)

The performance efficiency pillar includes the ability to use cloud resources efficiently to meet performance requirements, and to maintain that efficiency as demand changes and technologies evolve.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-dp.md): There are five design principles for performance efficiency in the cloud.
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-def.md): There are four best practice areas for performance efficiency in the cloud: selection, review, monitoring, and tradeoffs.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Architecture selection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-arch.md): The optimal solution for a particular workload varies, and solutions often combine multiple approaches.
- [Compute and hardware](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-compute.md): The optimal compute choice for a particular workload can vary based on application design, usage patterns, and configuration settings.
- [Data management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-data.md): The optimal data management solution for a particular system varies based on the kind of data type (block, file, or object), access patterns (random or sequential), required throughput, frequency of access (online, offline, archival), frequency of update (WORM, dynamic), and availability and durability constraints.
- [Networking and content delivery](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-networking.md): The optimal networking solution for a workload varies based on latency, throughput requirements, jitter, and bandwidth.
- [Process and culture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-process.md): When architecting workloads, there are principles and practices that you can adopt to help you better run efficient high-performing cloud workloads.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for Performance Efficiency.

### [Cost optimization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-optimization.md)

The Cost Optimization pillar includes the ability to run systems to deliver business value at the lowest price point.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-dp.md): There are five design principles for cost optimization in the cloud.
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-def.md): There are five best practice areas for cost optimization in the cloud.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Practice Cloud Financial Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-cfm.md): With the adoption of cloud, technology teams innovate faster due to shortened approval, procurement, and infrastructure deployment cycles.
- [Expenditure and usage awareness](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-aware.md): The increased flexibility and agility that the cloud provides encourages innovation and fast-paced development and deployment.
- [Cost-effective resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-cereso.md): Using the appropriate instances and resources for your workload is key to cost savings.
- [Manage demand and supply resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-mandem.md): When you move to the cloud, you pay only for what you need.
- [Optimize over time](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-opti.md): As AWS releases new services and features, it's a best practice to review your existing architectural decisions to verify they continue to be the most cost effective.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for Cost Optimization.

### [Sustainability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sustainability.md)

The Sustainability pillar includes understanding the impacts of the services used, quantifying impacts through the entire workload lifecycle, and applying design principles and best practices to reduce these impacts when building cloud workloads.

- [Design principles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-design-principles.md): There are six design principles for sustainability in the cloud:
- [Definition](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-def.md): There are six best practice areas for sustainability in the cloud.

### [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-bp.md)

Best practices

- [Region selection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-region-selection.md): The choice of Region for your workload significantly affects its KPIs, including performance, cost, and carbon footprint.
- [Alignment to demand](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-user-behavior-patterns.md): The way users and applications consume your workloads and other resources can help you identify improvements to meet sustainability goals.
- [Software and architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-software-architecture-patterns.md): Implement patterns for performing load smoothing and maintaining consistent high utilization of deployed resources to minimize the resources consumed.
- [Data management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-data-patterns.md): Implement data management practices to reduce the provisioned storage required to support your workload, and the resources required to use it.
- [Hardware and services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-hardware-patterns.md): Look for opportunities to reduce workload sustainability impacts by making changes to your hardware management practices.
- [Process and culture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-development-deployment-patterns.md): Look for opportunities to reduce your sustainability impact by making changes to your development, test, and deployment practices.
- [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-resources.md): Refer to the following resources to learn more about our best practices for sustainability.


## [Appendix: Questions and best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/appendix.md)

### [Operational excellence](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-operational-excellence.md)

Operational excellence (OE) is a commitment to build software correctly while consistently delivering a great customer experience.

### [Organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-organization.md)

Organization best practices

### [OPS 1. How do you determine what your priorities are?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-01.md)

Everyone should understand their part in enabling business success.

- [OPS01-BP01 Evaluate external customer needs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_ext_cust_needs.md): Involve key stakeholders, including business, development, and operations teams, to determine where to focus efforts on external customer needs.
- [OPS01-BP02 Evaluate internal customer needs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_int_cust_needs.md): Involve key stakeholders, including business, development, and operations teams, when determining where to focus efforts on internal customer needs.
- [OPS01-BP03 Evaluate governance requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_governance_reqs.md): Governance is the set of policies, rules, or frameworks that a company uses to achieve its business goals.
- [OPS01-BP04 Evaluate compliance requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_compliance_reqs.md): Regulatory, industry, and internal compliance requirements are an important driver for defining your organization’s priorities.
- [OPS01-BP05 Evaluate threat landscape](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_eval_threat_landscape.md): Evaluate threats to the business (for example, competition, business risk and liabilities, operational risks, and information security threats) and maintain current information in a risk registry.
- [OPS01-BP06 Evaluate tradeoffs while managing benefits and risks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_priorities_eval_tradeoffs.md): Competing interests from multiple parties can make it challenging to prioritize efforts, build capabilities, and deliver outcomes aligned with business strategies.

### [OPS 2. How do you structure your organization to support your business outcomes?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-02.md)

Your teams must understand their part in achieving business outcomes.

- [OPS02-BP01 Resources have identified owners](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_def_resource_owners.md): Resources for your workload must have identified owners for change control, troubleshooting, and other functions.
- [OPS02-BP02 Processes and procedures have identified owners](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_def_proc_owners.md): Understand who has ownership of the definition of individual processes and procedures, why those specific process and procedures are used, and why that ownership exists.
- [OPS02-BP03 Operations activities have identified owners responsible for their performance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_def_activity_owners.md): Understand who has responsibility to perform specific activities on defined workloads and why that responsibility exists.
- [OPS02-BP04 Mechanisms exist to manage responsibilities and ownership](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_def_responsibilities_ownership.md): Understand the responsibilities of your role and how you contribute to business outcomes, as this understanding informs the prioritization of your tasks and why your role is important.
- [OPS02-BP05 Mechanisms exist to request additions, changes, and exceptions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_req_add_chg_exception.md): You can make requests to owners of processes, procedures, and resources.
- [OPS02-BP06 Responsibilities between teams are predefined or negotiated](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ops_model_def_neg_team_agreements.md): Have defined or negotiated agreements between teams describing how they work with and support each other (for example, response times, service level objectives, or service-level agreements).

### [OPS 3. How does your organizational culture support your business outcomes?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-03.md)

Provide support for your team members so that they can be more effective in taking action and supporting your business outcome.

- [OPS03-BP01 Provide executive sponsorship](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_executive_sponsor.md): Senior leadership clearly sets expectations for the organization and evaluates success.
- [OPS03-BP02 Team members are empowered to take action when outcomes are at risk](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_team_emp_take_action.md): A cultural behavior of ownership instilled by leadership results in any employee feeling empowered to act on behalf of the entire company beyond their defined scope of role and accountability.
- [OPS03-BP03 Escalation is encouraged](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_team_enc_escalation.md): Team members are encouraged by leadership to escalate issues and concerns to higher-level decision makers and stakeholders if they believe desired outcomes are at risk and expected standards are not met.
- [OPS03-BP04 Communications are timely, clear, and actionable](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_effective_comms.md): Leadership is responsible for the creation of strong and effective communications, especially when the organization adopts new strategies, technologies, or ways of working.
- [OPS03-BP05 Experimentation is encouraged](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_team_enc_experiment.md): Experimentation is a catalyst for turning new ideas into products and features.
- [OPS03-BP06 Team members are encouraged to maintain and grow their skill sets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_team_enc_learn.md): Teams must grow their skill sets to adopt new technologies, and to support changes in demand and responsibilities in support of your workloads.
- [OPS03-BP07 Resource teams appropriately](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_org_culture_team_res_appro.md): Provision the right amount of proficient team members, and provide tools and resources to support your workload needs.

### [Prepare](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-prepare.md)

.

### [OPS 4. How do you implement observability in your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-04.md)

Implement observability in your workload so that you can understand its state and make data-driven decisions based on business requirements.

- [OPS04-BP01 Identify key performance indicators](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_observability_identify_kpis.md): Implementing observability in your workload starts with understanding its state and making data-driven decisions based on business requirements.
- [OPS04-BP02 Implement application telemetry](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_observability_application_telemetry.md): Application telemetry serves as the foundation for observability of your workload.
- [OPS04-BP03 Implement user experience telemetry](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_observability_customer_telemetry.md): Gaining deep insights into customer experiences and interactions with your application is crucial.
- [OPS04-BP04 Implement dependency telemetry](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_observability_dependency_telemetry.md): Dependency telemetry is essential for monitoring the health and performance of the external services and components your workload relies on.
- [OPS04-BP05 Implement distributed tracing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_observability_dist_trace.md): Distributed tracing offers a way to monitor and visualize requests as they traverse through various components of a distributed system.

### [OPS 5. How do you reduce defects, ease remediation, and improve flow into production?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-05.md)

Adopt approaches that improve flow of changes into production, that activate refactoring, fast feedback on quality, and bug fixing.

- [OPS05-BP01 Use version control](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_version_control.md): Use version control to activate tracking of changes and releases.
- [OPS05-BP02 Test and validate changes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_test_val_chg.md): Every change deployed must be tested to avoid errors in production.
- [OPS05-BP03 Use configuration management systems](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_conf_mgmt_sys.md): Use configuration management systems to make and track configuration changes.
- [OPS05-BP04 Use build and deployment management systems](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_build_mgmt_sys.md): Use build and deployment management systems.
- [OPS05-BP05 Perform patch management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_patch_mgmt.md): Perform patch management to gain features, address issues, and remain compliant with governance.
- [OPS05-BP06 Share design standards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_share_design_stds.md): Share best practices across teams to increase awareness and maximize the benefits of development efforts.
- [OPS05-BP07 Implement practices to improve code quality](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_code_quality.md): Implement practices to improve code quality and minimize defects.
- [OPS05-BP08 Use multiple environments](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_multi_env.md): Use multiple environments to experiment, develop, and test your workload.
- [OPS05-BP09 Make frequent, small, reversible changes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_freq_sm_rev_chg.md): Frequent, small, and reversible changes reduce the scope and impact of a change.
- [OPS05-BP10 Fully automate integration and deployment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_dev_integ_auto_integ_deploy.md): Automate build, deployment, and testing of the workload.

### [OPS 6. How do you mitigate deployment risks?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-06.md)

Adopt approaches that provide fast feedback on quality and achieve rapid recovery from changes that do not have desired outcomes.

- [OPS06-BP01 Plan for unsuccessful changes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_mit_deploy_risks_plan_for_unsucessful_changes.md): Plan to revert to a known good state, or remediate in the production environment if the deployment causes an undesired outcome.
- [OPS06-BP02 Test deployments](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_mit_deploy_risks_test_val_chg.md): Test release procedures in pre-production by using the same deployment configuration, security controls, steps, and procedures as in production.
- [OPS06-BP03 Employ safe deployment strategies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_mit_deploy_risks_deploy_mgmt_sys.md): Safe production roll-outs control the flow of beneficial changes with an aim to minimize any perceived impact for customers from those changes.
- [OPS06-BP04 Automate testing and rollback](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_mit_deploy_risks_auto_testing_and_rollback.md): To increase the speed, reliability, and confidence of your deployment process, have a strategy for automated testing and rollback capabilities in pre-production and production environments.

### [OPS 7. How do you know that you are ready to support a workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-07.md)

Evaluate the operational readiness of your workload, processes and procedures, and personnel to understand the operational risks related to your workload.

- [OPS07-BP01 Ensure personnel capability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_personnel_capability.md): Have a mechanism to validate that you have the appropriate number of trained personnel to support the workload.
- [OPS07-BP02: Ensure a consistent review of operational readiness](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_const_orr.md): Use Operational Readiness Reviews (ORRs) to validate that you can operate your workload.
- [OPS07-BP03 Use runbooks to perform procedures](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_use_runbooks.md): A runbook is a documented process to achieve a specific outcome.
- [OPS07-BP04 Use playbooks to investigate issues](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_use_playbooks.md): Playbooks are step-by-step guides used to investigate an incident.
- [OPS07-BP05 Make informed decisions to deploy systems and changes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_informed_deploy_decisions.md): Have processes in place for successful and unsuccessful changes to your workload.
- [OPS07-BP06 Create support plans for production workloads](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_ready_to_support_enable_support_plans.md): Create support for any software and services that your production workload relies on.

### [Operate](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-operate.md)

Operate questions and best practices

### [OPS 8. How do you utilize workload observability in your organization?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-08.md)

Ensure optimal workload health by leveraging observability.

- [OPS08-BP01 Analyze workload metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_workload_observability_analyze_workload_metrics.md): After implementing application telemetry, regularly analyze the collected metrics.
- [OPS08-BP02 Analyze workload logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_workload_observability_analyze_workload_logs.md): Regularly analyzing workload logs is essential for gaining a deeper understanding of the operational aspects of your application.
- [OPS08-BP03 Analyze workload traces](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_workload_observability_analyze_workload_traces.md): Analyzing trace data is crucial for achieving a comprehensive view of an application's operational journey.
- [OPS08-BP04 Create actionable alerts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_workload_observability_create_alerts.md): Promptly detecting and responding to deviations in your application's behavior is crucial.
- [OPS08-BP05 Create dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_workload_observability_create_dashboards.md): Dashboards are the human-centric view into the telemetry data of your workloads.

### [OPS 9. How do you understand the health of your operations?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-09.md)

Define, capture, and analyze operations metrics to gain visibility to operations events so that you can take appropriate action.

- [OPS09-BP01 Measure operations goals and KPIs with metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_operations_health_measure_ops_goals_kpis.md): Obtain goals and KPIs that define operations success from your organization and determine metrics that reflect these.
- [OPS09-BP02 Communicate status and trends to ensure visibility into operation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_operations_health_communicate_status_trends.md): Knowing the state of your operations and its trending direction is necessary to identify when outcomes may be at risk, whether or not added work can be supported, or the effects that changes have had to your teams.
- [OPS09-BP03 Review operations metrics and prioritize improvement](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_operations_health_review_ops_metrics_prioritize_improvement.md): Setting aside dedicated time and resources for reviewing the state of operations ensures that serving the day-to-day line of business remains a priority.

### [OPS 10. How do you manage workload and operations events?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-10.md)

Prepare and validate procedures for responding to events to minimize their disruption to your workload.

- [OPS10-BP01 Use a process for event, incident, and problem management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_event_incident_problem_process.md): The ability to efficiently manage events, incidents, and problems is key to maintaining workload health and performance.
- [OPS10-BP02 Have a process per alert](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_process_per_alert.md): Establishing a clear and defined process for each alert in your system is essential for effective and efficient incident management.
- [OPS10-BP03 Prioritize operational events based on business impact](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_prioritize_events.md): Responding promptly to operational events is critical, but not all events are equal.
- [OPS10-BP04 Define escalation paths](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_define_escalation_paths.md): Establish clear escalation paths within your incident response protocols to facilitate timely and effective action.
- [OPS10-BP05 Define a customer communication plan for service-impacting events](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_push_notify.md): Effective communication during service impacting events is critical to maintain trust and transparency with customers.
- [OPS10-BP06 Communicate status through dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_dashboards.md): Use dashboards as a strategic tool to convey real-time operational status and key metrics to different audiences, including internal technical teams, leadership, and customers.
- [OPS10-BP07 Automate responses to events](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_event_response_auto_event_response.md): Automating event responses is key for fast, consistent, and error-free operational handling.

### [Evolve](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-evolve.md)

Evolve questions and best practices

### [OPS 11. How do you evolve operations?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops-11.md)

Dedicate time and resources for nearly continuous incremental improvement to evolve the effectiveness and efficiency of your operations.

- [OPS11-BP01 Have a process for continuous improvement](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_process_cont_imp.md): Evaluate your workload against internal and external architecture best practices.
- [OPS11-BP02 Perform post-incident analysis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_perform_rca_process.md): Review customer-impacting events and identify the contributing factors and preventative actions.
- [OPS11-BP03 Implement feedback loops](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_feedback_loops.md): Feedback loops provide actionable insights that drive decision making.
- [OPS11-BP04 Perform knowledge management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_knowledge_management.md): Knowledge management helps team members find the information to perform their job.
- [OPS11-BP05 Define drivers for improvement](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_drivers_for_imp.md): Identify drivers for improvement to help you evaluate and prioritize opportunities based on data and feedback loops.
- [OPS11-BP06 Validate insights](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_validate_insights.md): Review your analysis results and responses with cross-functional teams and business owners.
- [OPS11-BP07 Perform operations metrics reviews](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_metrics_review.md): Regularly perform retrospective analysis of operations metrics with cross-team participants from different areas of the business.
- [OPS11-BP08 Document and share lessons learned](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_share_lessons_learned.md): Document and share lessons learned from the operations activities so that you can use them internally and across teams.
- [OPS11-BP09 Allocate time to make improvements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/ops_evolve_ops_allocate_time_for_imp.md): Dedicate time and resources within your processes to make continuous incremental improvements possible.

### [Security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-security.md)

The Security pillar encompasses the ability to protect data, systems, and assets to take advantage of cloud technologies to improve your security.

### [Security foundations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sec-security.md)

Security foundations questions and best practices

### [SEC 1. How do you securely operate your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-01.md)

To operate your workload securely, you must apply overarching best practices to every area of security.

- [SEC01-BP01 Separate workloads using accounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_multi_accounts.md): Establish common guardrails and isolation between environments (such as production, development, and test) and workloads through a multi-account strategy.
- [SEC01-BP02 Secure account root user and properties](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_aws_account.md): The root user is the most privileged user in an AWS account, with full administrative access to all resources within the account, and in some cases cannot be constrained by security policies.
- [SEC01-BP03 Identify and validate control objectives](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_control_objectives.md): Based on your compliance requirements and risks identified from your threat model, derive and validate the control objectives and controls that you need to apply to your workload.
- [SEC01-BP04 Stay up to date with security threats and recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_updated_threats.md): Stay up to date with the latest threats and mitigations by monitoring industry threat intelligence publications and data feeds for updates.
- [SEC01-BP05 Reduce security management scope](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_reduce_management_scope.md): Determine if you can reduce your security scope by using AWS services that shift management of certain controls to AWS (managed services).
- [SEC01-BP06 Automate deployment of standard security controls](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_automate_security_controls.md): Apply modern DevOps practices as you develop and deploy security controls that are standard across your AWS environments.  Define standard security controls and configurations using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates, capture changes in a version control system, test changes as part of a CI/CD pipeline, and automate the deployment of changes to your AWS environments.
- [SEC01-BP07 Identify threats and prioritize mitigations using a threat model](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_threat_model.md): Perform threat modeling to identify and maintain an up-to-date register of potential threats and associated mitigations for your workload.
- [SEC01-BP08 Evaluate and implement new security services and features regularly](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_securely_operate_implement_services_features.md): Evaluate and implement security services and features from AWS and AWS Partners that help you evolve the security posture of your workload. 

### [Identity and access management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-identity-and-access-management.md)

Identity and access management questions and best practices

### [SEC 2. How do you manage authentication for people and machines?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-02.md)

There are two types of identities that you must manage when approaching operating secure AWS workloads.

- [SEC02-BP01 Use strong sign-in mechanisms](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_enforce_mechanisms.md): Sign-ins (authentication using sign-in credentials) can present risks when not using mechanisms like multi-factor authentication (MFA), especially in situations where sign-in credentials have been inadvertently disclosed or are easily guessed.
- [SEC02-BP02 Use temporary credentials](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_unique.md): When doing any type of authentication, it’s best to use temporary credentials instead of long-term credentials to reduce or eliminate risks, such as credentials being inadvertently disclosed, shared, or stolen.
- [SEC02-BP03 Store and use secrets securely](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_secrets.md): A workload requires an automated capability to prove its identity to databases, resources, and third-party services.
- [SEC02-BP04 Rely on a centralized identity provider](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_identity_provider.md): For workforce identities (employees and contractors), rely on an identity provider that allows you to manage identities in a centralized place.
- [SEC02-BP05 Audit and rotate credentials periodically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_audit.md): Audit and rotate credentials periodically to limit how long the credentials can be used to access your resources.
- [SEC02-BP06 Employ user groups and attributes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_identities_groups_attributes.md): Defining permissions according to user groups and attributes helps reduce the number and complexity of policies, making it simpler to achieve the principle of least privilege.

### [SEC 3. How do you manage permissions for people and machines?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-03.md)

Manage permissions to control access to human and machine identities that require access to AWS and your workloads.

- [SEC03-BP01 Define access requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_define.md): Each component or resource of your workload needs to be accessed by administrators, end users, or other components.
- [SEC03-BP02 Grant least privilege access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_least_privileges.md): Grant only the access that users require to perform specific actions on specific resources under specific conditions.
- [SEC03-BP03 Establish emergency access process](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_emergency_process.md): Create a process that allows for emergency access to your workloads in the unlikely event of an issue with your centralized identity provider.
- [SEC03-BP04 Reduce permissions continuously](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_continuous_reduction.md): As your teams determine what access is required, remove unneeded permissions and establish review processes to achieve least privilege permissions.
- [SEC03-BP05 Define permission guardrails for your organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_define_guardrails.md): Use permission guardrails to reduce the scope of available permissions that can be granted to principals.
- [SEC03-BP06 Manage access based on lifecycle](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_lifecycle.md): Monitor and adjust the permissions granted to your principals (users, roles, and groups) throughout their lifecycle within your organization.
- [SEC03-BP07 Analyze public and cross-account access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_analyze_cross_account.md): Continually monitor findings that highlight public and cross-account access.
- [SEC03-BP08 Share resources securely within your organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_share_securely.md): As the number of workloads grows, you might need to share access to resources in those workloads or provision the resources multiple times across multiple accounts.
- [SEC03-BP09 Share resources securely with a third party](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_permissions_share_securely_third_party.md): The security of your cloud environment doesn't stop at your organization.

### [Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-detective-controls.md)

Detection questions and best practices

### [SEC 4. How do you detect and investigate security events?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-04.md)

Capture and analyze events from logs and metrics to gain visibility.

- [SEC04-BP01 Configure service and application logging](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_detect_investigate_events_app_service_logging.md): Retain security event logs from services and applications.
- [SEC04-BP02 Capture logs, findings, and metrics in standardized locations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_detect_investigate_events_logs.md): Security teams rely on logs and findings to analyze events that may indicate unauthorized activity or unintentional changes.
- [SEC04-BP03 Correlate and enrich security alerts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_detect_investigate_events_security_alerts.md): Unexpected activity can generate multiple security alerts by different sources, requiring further correlation and enrichment to understand the full context. Implement automated correlation and enrichment of security alerts to help achieve more accurate incident identification and response.
- [SEC04-BP04 Initiate remediation for non-compliant resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_detect_investigate_events_noncompliant_resources.md): Your detective controls may alert on resources that are out of compliance with your configuration requirements.

### [Infrastructure protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-infrastructure-protection.md)

Infrastructure protection questions and best practices

### [SEC 5. How do you protect your network resources?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-05.md)

Any workload that has some form of network connectivity, whether it’s the internet or a private network, requires multiple layers of defense to help protect from external and internal network-based threats.

- [SEC05-BP01 Create network layers](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_network_protection_create_layers.md): Segment your network topology into different layers based on logical groupings of your workload components according to their data sensitivity and access requirements.
- [SEC05-BP02 Control traffic flow within your network layers](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_network_protection_layered.md): Within the layers of your network, use further segmentation to restrict traffic only to the flows necessary for each workload.
- [SEC05-BP03 Implement inspection-based protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_network_protection_inspection.md): Set up traffic inspection points between your network layers to make sure data in transit matches the expected categories and patterns.  Analyze traffic flows, metadata, and patterns to help identify, detect, and respond to events more effectively.
- [SEC05-BP04 Automate network protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_network_auto_protect.md): Automate the deployment of your network protections using DevOps practices, such as infrastructure as code (IaC) and CI/CD pipelines.  These practices can help you track changes in your network protections through a version control system, reduce the time it takes to deploy changes, and help detect if your network protections drift from your desired configuration.  

### [SEC 6. How do you protect your compute resources?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-06.md)

Compute resources in your workload require multiple layers of defense to help protect from external and internal threats.

- [SEC06-BP01 Perform vulnerability management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_compute_vulnerability_management.md): Frequently scan and patch for vulnerabilities in your code, dependencies, and in your infrastructure to help protect against new threats.
- [SEC06-BP02 Provision compute from hardened images](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_compute_hardened_images.md): Provide fewer opportunities for unintended access to your runtime environments by deploying them from hardened images.
- [SEC06-BP03 Reduce manual management and interactive access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_compute_reduce_manual_management.md): Use automation to perform deployment, configuration, maintenance, and investigative tasks wherever possible.
- [SEC06-BP04 Validate software integrity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_compute_validate_software_integrity.md): Use cryptographic verification to validate the integrity of software artifacts (including images) your workload uses.  Cryptographically sign your software as a safeguard against unauthorized changes run within your compute environments.
- [SEC06-BP05 Automate compute protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_compute_auto_protection.md): Automate compute protection operations to reduce the need for human intervention.

### [Data protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-data-protection.md)

Questions

### [SEC 7. How do you classify your data?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-07.md)

Classification provides a way to categorize data, based on criticality and sensitivity in order to help you determine appropriate protection and retention controls.

- [SEC07-BP01 Understand your data classification scheme](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_data_classification_identify_data.md): Understand the classification of data your workload is processing, its handling requirements, the associated business processes, where the data is stored, and who the data owner is.  Your data classification and handling scheme should consider the applicable legal and compliance requirements of your workload and what data controls are needed.
- [SEC07-BP02 Apply data protection controls based on data sensitivity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_data_classification_define_protection.md): Apply data protection controls that provide an appropriate level of control for each class of data defined in your classification policy.  This practice can allow you to protect sensitive data from unauthorized access and use, while preserving the availability and use of data.
- [SEC07-BP03 Automate identification and classification](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_data_classification_auto_classification.md): Automating the identification and classification of data can help you implement the correct controls.
- [SEC07-BP04 Define scalable data lifecycle management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_data_classification_lifecycle_management.md): Understand your data lifecycle requirements as they relate to your different levels of data classification and handling.  This can include how data is handled when it first enters your environment, how data is transformed, and the rules for its destruction. Consider factors such as retention periods, access, auditing, and tracking provenance.

### [SEC 8. How do you protect your data at rest?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-08.md)

Protect your data at rest by implementing multiple controls, to reduce the risk of unauthorized access or mishandling.

- [SEC08-BP01 Implement secure key management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_rest_key_mgmt.md): Secure key management includes the storage, rotation, access control, and monitoring of key material required to secure data at rest for your workload.
- [SEC08-BP02 Enforce encryption at rest](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_rest_encrypt.md): Encrypt private data at rest to maintain confidentiality and provide an additional layer of protection against unintended data disclosure or exfiltration.
- [SEC08-BP03 Automate data at rest protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_rest_automate_protection.md): Use automation to validate and enforce data at rest controls.  Use automated scanning to detect misconfiguration of your data storage solutions, and perform remediations through automated programmatic response where possible.  Incorporate automation in your CI/CD processes to detect data storage misconfigurations before they are deployed to production.
- [SEC08-BP04 Enforce access control](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_rest_access_control.md): To help protect your data at rest, enforce access control using mechanisms such as isolation and versioning.

### [SEC 9. How do you protect your data in transit?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-09.md)

Protect your data in transit by implementing multiple controls to reduce the risk of unauthorized access or loss.

- [SEC09-BP01 Implement secure key and certificate management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_transit_key_cert_mgmt.md): Transport Layer Security (TLS) certificates are used to secure network communications and establish the identity of websites, resources, and workloads over the internet, as well as private networks.
- [SEC09-BP02 Enforce encryption in transit](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_transit_encrypt.md): Enforce your defined encryption requirements based on your organization’s policies, regulatory obligations and standards to help meet organizational, legal, and compliance requirements.
- [SEC09-BP03 Authenticate network communications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_protect_data_transit_authentication.md): Verify the identity of communications by using protocols that support authentication, such as Transport Layer Security (TLS) or IPsec.

### [Incident response](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-incident-response.md)

Question

### [SEC 10. How do you anticipate, respond to, and recover from incidents?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-10.md)

Even with mature preventive and detective controls, your organization should implement mechanisms to respond to and mitigate the potential impact of security incidents.

- [SEC10-BP01 Identify key personnel and external resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_identify_personnel.md): Identify internal and external personnel, resources, and legal obligations to help your organization respond to an incident.
- [SEC10-BP02 Develop incident management plans](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_develop_management_plans.md): The first document to develop for incident response is the incident response plan.
- [SEC10-BP03 Prepare forensic capabilities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_prepare_forensic.md): Ahead of a security incident, consider developing forensics capabilities to support security event investigations.
- [SEC10-BP04 Develop and test security incident response playbooks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_playbooks.md): A key part of preparing your incident response processes is developing playbooks.
- [SEC10-BP05 Pre-provision access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_pre_provision_access.md): Verify that incident responders have the correct access pre-provisioned in AWS to reduce the time needed for investigation through to recovery.
- [SEC10-BP06 Pre-deploy tools](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_pre_deploy_tools.md): Verify that security personnel have the right tools pre-deployed to reduce the time for investigation through to recovery.
- [SEC10-BP07 Run simulations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_run_game_days.md): As organizations grow and evolve over time, so does the threat landscape, making it important to continually review your incident response capabilities.
- [SEC10-BP08 Establish a framework for learning from incidents](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_incident_response_establish_incident_framework.md): Implementing a lessons learned framework and root cause analysis capability will not only help improve incident response capabilities, but also help prevent the incident from recurring.

### [Application security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-appsec.md)

Question

### [SEC 11. How do you incorporate and validate the security properties of applications throughout the design, development, and deployment lifecycle?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec-11.md)

Training people, testing using automation, understanding dependencies, and validating the security properties of tools and applications help to reduce the likelihood of security issues in production workloads.

- [SEC11-BP01 Train for application security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_train_for_application_security.md): Provide training to the builders in your organization on common practices for the secure development and operation of applications.
- [SEC11-BP02 Automate testing throughout the development and release lifecycle](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_automate_testing_throughout_lifecycle.md): Automate the testing for security properties throughout the development and release lifecycle.
- [SEC11-BP03 Perform regular penetration testing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_perform_regular_penetration_testing.md): Perform regular penetration testing of your software.
- [SEC11-BP04 Conduct code reviews](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_manual_code_reviews.md): Implement code reviews to help verify the quality and security of software being developed.
- [SEC11-BP05 Centralize services for packages and dependencies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_centralize_services_for_packages_and_dependencies.md): Provide centralized services for your teams to obtain software packages and other dependencies.
- [SEC11-BP06 Deploy software programmatically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_deploy_software_programmatically.md): Perform software deployments programmatically where possible.
- [SEC11-BP07 Regularly assess security properties of the pipelines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_regularly_assess_security_properties_of_pipelines.md): Apply the principles of the Well-Architected Security Pillar to your pipelines, with particular attention to the separation of permissions.
- [SEC11-BP08 Build a program that embeds security ownership in workload teams](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sec_appsec_build_program_that_embeds_security_ownership_in_teams.md): Build a program or mechanism that empowers builder teams to make security decisions about the software that they create.

### [Reliability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-reliability.md)

The Reliability pillar encompasses the ability of a workload to perform its intended function correctly and consistently when it’s expected to.

### [Foundations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-foundations.md)

Foundations questions and best practices

### [REL 1. How do you manage Service Quotas and constraints?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-01.md)

For cloud-based workload architectures, there are Service Quotas (which are also referred to as service limits).

- [REL01-BP01 Aware of service quotas and constraints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_aware_quotas_and_constraints.md): Be aware of your default quotas and manage your quota increase requests for your workload architecture.
- [REL01-BP02 Manage service quotas across accounts and regions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_limits_considered.md): If you are using multiple accounts or Regions, request the appropriate quotas in all environments in which your production workloads run.
- [REL01-BP03 Accommodate fixed service quotas and constraints through architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_aware_fixed_limits.md): Be aware of unchangeable service quotas, service constraints, and physical resource limits.
- [REL01-BP04 Monitor and manage quotas](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_monitor_manage_limits.md): Evaluate your potential usage and increase your quotas appropriately, allowing for planned growth in usage.
- [REL01-BP05 Automate quota management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_automated_monitor_limits.md): Service quotas, also referred to as limits in AWS services, are the maximum values for the resources in your AWS account.
- [REL01-BP06 Ensure that a sufficient gap exists between the current quotas and the maximum usage to accommodate failover](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_manage_service_limits_suff_buffer_limits.md): This article explains how to maintain space between the resource quota and your usage, and how it can benefit your organization.

### [REL 2. How do you plan your network topology?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-02.md)

Workloads often exist in multiple environments.

- [REL02-BP01 Use highly available network connectivity for your workload public endpoints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_ha_conn_users.md): Building highly available network connectivity to public endpoints of your workloads can help you reduce downtime due to loss of connectivity and improve the availability and SLA of your workload.
- [REL02-BP02 Provision redundant connectivity between private networks in the cloud and on-premises environments](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_ha_conn_private_networks.md): Implement redundancy in your connections between private networks in the cloud and on-premises environments to achieve connectivity resilience.
- [REL02-BP03 Ensure IP subnet allocation accounts for expansion and availability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_ip_subnet_allocation.md): Amazon VPC IP address ranges must be large enough to accommodate workload requirements, including factoring in future expansion and allocation of IP addresses to subnets across Availability Zones.
- [REL02-BP04 Prefer hub-and-spoke topologies over many-to-many mesh](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_prefer_hub_and_spoke.md): When connecting multiple private networks, such as Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) and on-premises networks, opt for a hub-and-spoke topology over a meshed one.
- [REL02-BP05 Enforce non-overlapping private IP address ranges in all private address spaces where they are connected](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_non_overlap_ip.md): The IP address ranges of each of your VPCs must not overlap when peered, connected via Transit Gateway, or connected over VPN.

### [Workload architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-workload-architecture.md)

Workload architecture questions and best practices

### [REL 3. How do you design your workload service architecture?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-03.md)

Build highly scalable and reliable workloads using a service-oriented architecture (SOA) or a microservices architecture.

- [REL03-BP01 Choose how to segment your workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_service_architecture_monolith_soa_microservice.md): Workload segmentation is important when determining the resilience requirements of your application.
- [REL03-BP02 Build services focused on specific business domains and functionality](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_service_architecture_business_domains.md): Service-oriented architectures (SOA) define services with well-delineated functions defined by business needs.
- [REL03-BP03 Provide service contracts per API](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_service_architecture_api_contracts.md): Service contracts are documented agreements between API producers and consumers defined in a machine-readable API definition.

### [REL 4. How do you design interactions in a distributed system to prevent failures?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-04.md)

Distributed systems rely on communications networks to interconnect components, such as servers or services.

- [REL04-BP01 Identify the kind of distributed systems you depend on](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_prevent_interaction_failure_identify.md): Hard real-time distributed systems require responses to be given synchronously and rapidly, while soft real-time systems have a more generous time window of minutes or more for response.
- [REL04-BP02 Implement loosely coupled dependencies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_prevent_interaction_failure_loosely_coupled_system.md): Dependencies such as queuing systems, streaming systems, workflows, and load balancers are loosely coupled.
- [REL04-BP03 Do constant work](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_prevent_interaction_failure_constant_work.md): Systems can fail when there are large, rapid changes in load.
- [REL04-BP04 Make mutating operations idempotent](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_prevent_interaction_failure_idempotent.md): An idempotent service promises that each request is processed exactly once, such that making multiple identical requests has the same effect as making a single request.

### [REL 5. How do you design interactions in a distributed system to mitigate or withstand failures?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-05.md)

Distributed systems rely on communications networks to interconnect components (such as servers or services).

- [REL05-BP01 Implement graceful degradation to transform applicable hard dependencies into soft dependencies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_graceful_degradation.md): Application components should continue to perform their core function even if dependencies become unavailable.
- [REL05-BP02 Throttle requests](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_throttle_requests.md): Throttle requests to mitigate resource exhaustion due to unexpected increases in demand.
- [REL05-BP03 Control and limit retry calls](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_limit_retries.md): Use exponential backoff to retry requests at progressively longer intervals between each retry.
- [REL05-BP04 Fail fast and limit queues](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_fail_fast.md): When a service is unable to respond successfully to a request, fail fast.
- [REL05-BP05 Set client timeouts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_client_timeouts.md): Set timeouts appropriately on connections and requests, verify them systematically, and do not rely on default values as they are not aware of workload specifics.
- [REL05-BP06 Make systems stateless where possible](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_stateless.md): Systems should either not require state, or should offload state such that between different client requests, there is no dependence on locally stored data on disk and in memory.
- [REL05-BP07 Implement emergency levers](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_emergency_levers.md): Emergency levers are rapid processes that can mitigate availability impact on your workload.

### [Change management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-change-management.md)

Change management questions and best practices

### [REL 6. How do you monitor workload resources?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-06.md)

Logs and metrics are powerful tools to gain insight into the health of your workload.

- [REL06-BP01 Monitor all components for the workload (Generation)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_monitor_resources.md): Monitor the components of the workload with Amazon CloudWatch or third-party tools.
- [REL06-BP02 Define and calculate metrics (Aggregation)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_notification_aggregation.md): Collect metrics and logs from your workload components and calculate relevant aggregate metrics from them.
- [REL06-BP03 Send notifications (Real-time processing and alarming)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_notification_monitor.md): When organizations detect potential issues, they send real-time notifications and alerts to the appropriate personnel and systems in order to respond quickly and effectively to these issues.
- [REL06-BP04 Automate responses (Real-time processing and alarming)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_automate_response_monitor.md): Use automation to take action when an event is detected, for example, to replace failed components.
- [REL06-BP05 Analyze logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_storage_analytics.md): Collect log files and metrics histories and analyze these for broader trends and workload insights.
- [REL06-BP06 Regularly review monitoring scope and metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_review_monitoring.md): Frequently review how workload monitoring is implemented, and update it as your workload and its architecture evolves.
- [REL06-BP07 Monitor end-to-end tracing of requests through your system](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_monitor_aws_resources_end_to_end.md): Trace requests as they process through service components so product teams can more easily analyze and debug issues and improve performance.

### [REL 7. How do you design your workload to adapt to changes in demand?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-07.md)

A scalable workload provides elasticity to add or remove resources automatically so that they closely match the current demand at any given point in time.

- [REL07-BP01 Use automation when obtaining or scaling resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_adapt_to_changes_autoscale_adapt.md): A cornerstone of reliability in the cloud is the programmatic definition, provisioning, and management of your infrastructure and resources.
- [REL07-BP02 Obtain resources upon detection of impairment to a workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_adapt_to_changes_reactive_adapt_auto.md): Scale resources reactively when necessary if availability is impacted, to restore workload availability.
- [REL07-BP03 Obtain resources upon detection that more resources are needed for a workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_adapt_to_changes_proactive_adapt_auto.md): One of the most valuable features of cloud computing is the ability to provision resources dynamically.
- [REL07-BP04 Load test your workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_adapt_to_changes_load_tested_adapt.md): Adopt a load testing methodology to measure if scaling activity meets workload requirements.

### [REL 8. How do you implement change?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-08.md)

Controlled changes are necessary to deploy new functionality, and to verify that the workloads and the operating environment are running known software and can be patched or replaced in a predictable manner.

- [REL08-BP01 Use runbooks for standard activities such as deployment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_tracking_change_management_planned_changemgmt.md): Runbooks are the predefined procedures to achieve specific outcomes.
- [REL08-BP02 Integrate functional testing as part of your deployment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_tracking_change_management_functional_testing.md): Use techniques such as unit tests and integration tests that validate required functionality.
- [REL08-BP03 Integrate resiliency testing as part of your deployment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_tracking_change_management_resiliency_testing.md): Integrate resiliency testing by consciously introducing failures in your system to measure its capability in case of disruptive scenarios.
- [REL08-BP04 Deploy using immutable infrastructure](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_tracking_change_management_immutable_infrastructure.md): Immutable infrastructure is a model that mandates that no updates, security patches, or configuration changes happen in-place on production workloads.
- [REL08-BP05 Deploy changes with automation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_tracking_change_management_automated_changemgmt.md): Deployments and patching are automated to eliminate negative impact.

### [Failure management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-failure-management.md)

Failure management questions and best practices

### [REL 9. How do you back up data?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-09.md)

Back up data, applications, and configuration to meet your requirements for recovery time objectives (RTO) and recovery point objectives (RPO).

- [REL09-BP01 Identify and back up all data that needs to be backed up, or reproduce the data from sources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_backing_up_data_identified_backups_data.md): Understand and use the backup capabilities of the data services and resources used by the workload.
- [REL09-BP02 Secure and encrypt backups](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_backing_up_data_secured_backups_data.md): Control and detect access to backups using authentication and authorization.
- [REL09-BP03 Perform data backup automatically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_backing_up_data_automated_backups_data.md): Configure backups to be taken automatically based on a periodic schedule informed by the Recovery Point Objective (RPO), or by changes in the dataset.
- [REL09-BP04 Perform periodic recovery of the data to verify backup integrity and processes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_backing_up_data_periodic_recovery_testing_data.md): Validate that your backup process implementation meets your Recovery Time Objectives (RTO) and Recovery Point Objectives (RPO) by performing a recovery test.

### [REL 10. How do you use fault isolation to protect your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-10.md)

Fault isolation limits the impact of a component or system failure to a defined boundary.

- [REL10-BP01 Deploy the workload to multiple locations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_fault_isolation_multiaz_region_system.md): Distribute workload data and resources across multiple Availability Zones or, where necessary, across AWS Regions.
- [REL10-BP02 Automate recovery for components constrained to a single location](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_fault_isolation_single_az_system.md): If components of the workload can only run in a single Availability Zone or in an on-premises data center, implement the capability to do a complete rebuild of the workload within your defined recovery objectives.
- [REL10-BP03 Use bulkhead architectures to limit scope of impact](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_fault_isolation_use_bulkhead.md): Implement bulkhead architectures (also known as cell-based architectures) to restrict the effect of failure within a workload to a limited number of components.

### [REL 11. How do you design your workload to withstand component failures?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-11.md)

Workloads with a requirement for high availability and low mean time to recovery (MTTR) must be architected for resiliency.

- [REL11-BP01 Monitor all components of the workload to detect failures](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_monitoring_health.md): Continuously monitor the health of your workload so that you and your automated systems are aware of degradation or failure as soon as they occur.
- [REL11-BP02 Fail over to healthy resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_failover2good.md): If a resource failure occurs, healthy resources should continue to serve requests.
- [REL11-BP03 Automate healing on all layers](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_auto_healing_system.md): Upon detection of a failure, use automated capabilities to perform actions to remediate.
- [REL11-BP04 Rely on the data plane and not the control plane during recovery](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_avoid_control_plane.md): Control planes provide the administrative APIs used to create, read and describe, update, delete, and list (CRUDL) resources, while data planes handle day-to-day service traffic.
- [REL11-BP05 Use static stability to prevent bimodal behavior](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_static_stability.md): Workloads should be statically stable and only operate in a single normal mode.
- [REL11-BP06 Send notifications when events impact availability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_notifications_sent_system.md): Notifications are sent upon the detection of thresholds breached, even if the event causing the issue was automatically resolved.
- [REL11-BP07 Architect your product to meet availability targets and uptime service level agreements (SLAs)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_withstand_component_failures_service_level_agreements.md): Architect your product to meet availability targets and uptime service level agreements (SLAs).

### [REL 12. How do you test reliability?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-12.md)

After you have designed your workload to be resilient to the stresses of production, testing is the only way to verify that it will operate as designed, and deliver the resiliency you expect.

- [REL12-BP01 Use playbooks to investigate failures](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_testing_resiliency_playbook_resiliency.md): Permit consistent and prompt responses to failure scenarios that are not well understood, by documenting the investigation process in playbooks.
- [REL12-BP02 Perform post-incident analysis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_testing_resiliency_rca_resiliency.md): Review customer-impacting events, and identify the contributing factors and preventative action items.
- [REL12-BP03 Test scalability and performance requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_testing_resiliency_test_non_functional.md): Use techniques such as load testing to validate that the workload meets scaling and performance requirements.
- [REL12-BP04 Test resiliency using chaos engineering](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_testing_resiliency_failure_injection_resiliency.md): Run chaos experiments regularly in environments that are in or as close to production as possible to understand how your system responds to adverse conditions.
- [REL12-BP05 Conduct game days regularly](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_testing_resiliency_game_days_resiliency.md): Conduct game days to regularly exercise your procedures for responding to workload-impacting events and impairments.

### [REL 13. How do you plan for disaster recovery (DR)?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel-13.md)

Having backups and redundant workload components in place is the start of your DR strategy.

- [REL13-BP01 Define recovery objectives for downtime and data loss](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_objective_defined_recovery.md): Failures can impact your business in several ways.
- [REL13-BP02 Use defined recovery strategies to meet the recovery objectives](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_disaster_recovery.md): Define a disaster recovery (DR) strategy that meets your workload's recovery objectives.
- [REL13-BP03 Test disaster recovery implementation to validate the implementation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_dr_tested.md): Regularly test failover to your recovery site to verify that it operates properly and that RTO and RPO are met.
- [REL13-BP04 Manage configuration drift at the DR site or Region](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_config_drift.md): To perform a successful disaster recovery (DR) procedure, your workload must be able to resume normal operations in a timely manner with no relevant loss of functionality or data once the DR environment has been brought online.
- [REL13-BP05 Automate recovery](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_auto_recovery.md): Implement tested and automated recovery mechanisms that are reliable, observable, and reproducible to reduce the risk and business impact of failure.

### [Performance efficiency](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-performance-efficiency.md)

The Performance Efficiency pillar includes the ability to use computing resources efficiently to meet system requirements, and to maintain that efficiency as demand changes and technologies evolve.

### [Architecture selection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-selection.md)

Architecture selection best practices and questions

### [PERF 1. How do you select appropriate cloud resources and architecture for your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-01.md)

The optimal solution for a particular workload varies, and solutions often combine multiple approaches.

- [PERF01-BP01 Learn about and understand available cloud services and features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_understand_cloud_services_and_features.md): Continually learn about and discover available services and configurations that help you make better architectural decisions and improve performance efficiency in your workload architecture.
- [PERF01-BP02 Use guidance from your cloud provider or an appropriate partner to learn about architecture patterns and best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_guidance_architecture_patterns_best_practices.md): Use cloud company resources such as documentation, solutions architects, professional services, or appropriate partners to guide your architectural decisions.
- [PERF01-BP03 Factor cost into architectural decisions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_factor_cost_into_architectural_decisions.md): Factor cost into your architectural decisions to improve resource utilization and performance efficiency of your cloud workload.
- [PERF01-BP04 Evaluate how trade-offs impact customers and architecture efficiency](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_evaluate_trade_offs.md): When evaluating performance-related improvements, determine which choices impact your customers and workload efficiency.
- [PERF01-BP05 Use policies and reference architectures](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_use_policies_and_reference_architectures.md): Use internal policies and existing reference architectures when selecting services and configurations to be more efficient when designing and implementing your workload.
- [PERF01-BP06 Use benchmarking to drive architectural decisions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_use_benchmarking.md): Benchmark the performance of an existing workload to understand how it performs on the cloud and drive architectural decisions based on that data.
- [PERF01-BP07 Use a data-driven approach for architectural choices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_architecture_use_data_driven_approach.md): Define a clear, data-driven approach for architectural choices to verify that the right cloud services and configurations are used to meet your specific business needs.

### [Compute and hardware](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-compute-hardware.md)

Compute and hardware best practices and questions

### [PERF 2. How do you select and use compute resources in your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-02.md)

The optimal compute choice for a particular workload can vary based on application design, usage patterns, and configuration settings.

- [PERF02-BP01 Select the best compute options for your workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_select_best_compute_options.md): Selecting the most appropriate compute option for your workload allows you to improve performance, reduce unnecessary infrastructure costs, and lower the operational efforts required to maintain your workload.
- [PERF02-BP02 Understand the available compute configuration and features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_understand_compute_configuration_features.md): Understand the available configuration options and features for your compute service to help you provision the right amount of resources and improve performance efficiency.
- [PERF02-BP03 Collect compute-related metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_collect_compute_related_metrics.md): Record and track compute-related metrics to better understand how your compute resources are performing and improve their performance and their utilization.
- [PERF02-BP04 Configure and right-size compute resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_configure_and_right_size_compute_resources.md): Configure and right-size compute resources to match your workload’s performance requirements and avoid under- or over-utilized resources.
- [PERF02-BP05 Scale your compute resources dynamically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_scale_compute_resources_dynamically.md): Use the elasticity of the cloud to scale your compute resources up or down dynamically to match your needs and avoid over- or under-provisioning capacity for your workload.
- [PERF02-BP06 Use optimized hardware-based compute accelerators](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_compute_hardware_compute_accelerators.md): Use hardware accelerators to perform certain functions more efficiently than CPU-based alternatives.

### [Data management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-data-management.md)

Data management best practices and questions

### [PERF 3. How do you store, manage, and access data in your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-03.md)

The optimal data management solution for a particular system varies based on the kind of data type (block, file, or object), access patterns (random or sequential), required throughput, frequency of access (online, offline, archival), frequency of update (WORM, dynamic), and availability and durability constraints.

- [PERF03-BP01 Use a purpose-built data store that best supports your data access and storage requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_data_use_purpose_built_data_store.md): Understand data characteristics (like shareable, size, cache size, access patterns, latency, throughput, and persistence of data) to select the right purpose-built data stores (storage or database) for your workload.
- [PERF03-BP02 Evaluate available configuration options for data store](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_data_evaluate_configuration_options_data_store.md): Understand and evaluate the various features and configuration options available for your data stores to optimize storage space and performance for your workload.
- [PERF03-BP03 Collect and record data store performance metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_data_collect_record_data_store_performance_metrics.md): Track and record relevant performance metrics for your data store to understand how your data management solutions are performing.
- [PERF03-BP04 Implement strategies to improve query performance in data store](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_data_implement_strategies_to_improve_query_performance.md): Implement strategies to optimize data and improve data query to enable more scalability and efficient performance for your workload.
- [PERF03-BP05 Implement data access patterns that utilize caching](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_data_access_patterns_caching.md): Implement access patterns that can benefit from caching data for fast retrieval of frequently accessed data.

### [Networking and content delivery](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-networking-delivery.md)

Networking and content delivery best practices and questions

### [PERF 4. How do you select and configure networking resources in your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-04.md)

The optimal networking solution for a workload varies based on latency, throughput requirements, jitter, and bandwidth.

- [PERF04-BP01 Understand how networking impacts performance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_understand_how_networking_impacts_performance.md): Analyze and understand how network-related decisions impact your workload to provide efficient performance and improved user experience.
- [PERF04-BP02 Evaluate available networking features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_evaluate_networking_features.md): Evaluate networking features in the cloud that may increase performance.
- [PERF04-BP03 Choose appropriate dedicated connectivity or VPN for your workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_choose_appropriate_dedicated_connectivity_or_vpn.md): When hybrid connectivity is required to connect on-premises and cloud resources, provision adequate bandwidth to meet your performance requirements.
- [PERF04-BP04 Use load balancing to distribute traffic across multiple resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_load_balancing_distribute_traffic.md): Distribute traffic across multiple resources or services to allow your workload to take advantage of the elasticity that the cloud provides.
- [PERF04-BP05 Choose network protocols to improve performance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_choose_network_protocols_improve_performance.md): Make decisions about protocols for communication between systems and networks based on the impact to the workload’s performance.
- [PERF04-BP06 Choose your workload's location based on network requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_choose_workload_location_network_requirements.md): Evaluate options for resource placement to reduce network latency and improve throughput, providing an optimal user experience by reducing page load and data transfer times.
- [PERF04-BP07 Optimize network configuration based on metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_networking_optimize_network_configuration_based_on_metrics.md): Use collected and analyzed data to make informed decisions about optimizing your network configuration.

### [Process and culture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-process-culture.md)

Process and culture best practices and questions

### [PERF 5. How do your organizational practices and culture contribute to performance efficiency in your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf-05.md)

When architecting workloads, there are principles and practices that you can adopt to help you better run efficient high-performing cloud workloads.

- [PERF05-BP01 Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure workload health and performance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_establish_key_performance_indicators.md): Identify the KPIs that quantitatively and qualitatively measure workload performance.
- [PERF05-BP02 Use monitoring solutions to understand the areas where performance is most critical](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_use_monitoring_solutions.md): Understand and identify areas where increasing the performance of your workload will have a positive impact on efficiency or customer experience.
- [PERF05-BP03 Define a process to improve workload performance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_workload_performance.md): Define a process to evaluate new services, design patterns, resource types, and configurations as they become available.
- [PERF05-BP04 Load test your workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_load_test.md): Load test your workload to verify it can handle production load and identify any performance bottleneck.
- [PERF05-BP05 Use automation to proactively remediate performance-related issues](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_automation_remediate_issues.md): Use key performance indicators (KPIs), combined with monitoring and alerting systems, to proactively address performance-related issues.
- [PERF05-BP06 Keep your workload and services up-to-date](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_keep_workload_and_services_up_to_date.md): Stay up-to-date on new cloud services and features to adopt efficient features, remove issues, and improve the overall performance efficiency of your workload.
- [PERF05-BP07 Review metrics at regular intervals](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/perf_process_culture_review_metrics.md): As part of routine maintenance or in response to events or incidents, review which metrics are collected.

### [Cost optimization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-cost-optimization.md)

The Cost Optimization pillar includes the ability to run systems to deliver business value at the lowest price point.

### [Practice Cloud Financial Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-practice-cloud-financial-management.md)

Practice Cloud Financial Management questions and best practices

### [COST 1. How do you implement cloud financial management?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-01.md)

Implementing Cloud Financial Management helps organizations realize business value and financial success as they optimize their cost and usage and scale on AWS.

- [COST01-BP01 Establish ownership of cost optimization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_function.md): Create a team (Cloud Business Office, Cloud Center of Excellence, or FinOps) that is responsible for establishing and maintaining cost awareness across your organization.
- [COST01-BP02 Establish a partnership between finance and technology](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_partnership.md): Involve finance and technology teams in cost and usage discussions at all stages of your cloud journey.
- [COST01-BP03 Establish cloud budgets and forecasts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_budget_forecast.md): Adjust existing organizational budgeting and forecasting processes to be compatible with the highly variable nature of cloud costs and usage.
- [COST01-BP04 Implement cost awareness in your organizational processes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_cost_awareness.md): Implement cost awareness, create transparency, and accountability of costs into new or existing processes that impact usage, and leverage existing processes for cost awareness.
- [COST01-BP05 Report and notify on cost optimization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_usage_report.md): Set up cloud budgets and configure mechanisms to detect anomalies in usage.
- [COST01-BP06 Monitor cost proactively](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_proactive_process.md): Implement tooling and dashboards to monitor cost proactively for the workload.
- [COST01-BP07 Keep up-to-date with new service releases](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_scheduled.md): Consult regularly with experts or AWS Partners to consider which services and features provide lower cost.
- [COST01-BP08 Create a cost-aware culture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_culture.md): Implement changes or programs across your organization to create a cost-aware culture.
- [COST01-BP09 Quantify business value from cost optimization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_cloud_financial_management_quantify_value.md): Quantifying business value from cost optimization allows you to understand the entire set of benefits to your organization.

### [Expenditure and usage awareness](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-expenditure-and-usage-awareness.md)

Expenditure and usage awareness question and best practices

### [COST 2. How do you govern usage?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-02.md)

Establish policies and mechanisms to verify that appropriate costs are incurred while objectives are achieved.

- [COST02-BP01 Develop policies based on your organization requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_policies.md): Develop policies that define how resources are managed by your organization and inspect them periodically.
- [COST02-BP02 Implement goals and targets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_goal_target.md): Implement both cost and usage goals and targets for your workload.
- [COST02-BP03 Implement an account structure](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_account_structure.md): Implement a structure of accounts that maps to your organization.
- [COST02-BP04 Implement groups and roles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_groups_roles.md): Implement groups and roles that align to your policies and control who can create, modify, or decommission instances and resources in each group.
- [COST02-BP05 Implement cost controls](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_controls.md): Implement controls based on organization policies and defined groups and roles.
- [COST02-BP06 Track project lifecycle](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_govern_usage_track_lifecycle.md): Track, measure, and audit the lifecycle of projects, teams, and environments to avoid using and paying for unnecessary resources.

### [COST 3. How do you monitor your cost and usage?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-03.md)

Establish policies and procedures to monitor and appropriately allocate your costs.

- [COST03-BP01 Configure detailed information sources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_detailed_source.md): Set up cost management and reporting tools for enhanced analysis and transparency of cost and usage data.
- [COST03-BP02 Add organization information to cost and usage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_org_information.md): Define a tagging schema based on your organization, workload attributes, and cost allocation categories so that you can filter and search for resources or monitor cost and usage in cost management tools.
- [COST03-BP03 Identify cost attribution categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_define_attribution.md): Identify organization categories such as business units, departments or projects that could be used to allocate cost within your organization to the internal consuming entities.
- [COST03-BP04 Establish organization metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_define_kpi.md): Establish the organization metrics that are required for this workload.
- [COST03-BP05 Configure billing and cost management tools](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_config_tools.md): Configure cost management tools that meet your organization's policies to manage and optimize cloud spending.
- [COST03-BP06 Allocate costs based on workload metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_monitor_usage_allocate_outcome.md): Allocate the workload's costs based on usage metrics or business outcomes to measure workload cost efficiency.

### [COST 4. How do you decommission resources?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-04.md)

Implement change control and resource management from project inception to end-of-life.

- [COST04-BP01 Track resources over their lifetime](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_decomissioning_resources_track.md): Define and implement a method to track resources and their associations with systems over their lifetime.
- [COST04-BP02 Implement a decommissioning process](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_decomissioning_resources_implement_process.md): Implement a process to identify and decommission unused resources.
- [COST04-BP03 Decommission resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_decomissioning_resources_decommission.md): Decommission resources initiated by events such as periodic audits, or changes in usage.
- [COST04-BP04 Decommission resources automatically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_decomissioning_resources_decomm_automated.md): Design your workload to gracefully handle resource termination as you identify and decommission non-critical resources, resources that are not required, or resources with low utilization.
- [COST04-BP05 Enforce data retention policies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_decomissioning_resources_data_retention.md): Define data retention policies on supported resources to handle object deletion per your organizations’ requirements.

### [Cost-effective resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-cost-effective-resources.md)

Cost-effective resources questions and best practices

### [COST 5. How do you evaluate cost when you select services?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-05.md)

Amazon EC2, Amazon EBS, and Amazon S3 are building-block AWS services.

- [COST05-BP01 Identify organization requirements for cost](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_requirements.md): Work with team members to define the balance between cost optimization and other pillars, such as performance and reliability, for this workload.
- [COST05-BP02 Analyze all components of the workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_analyze_all.md): Verify every workload component is analyzed, regardless of current size or current costs.
- [COST05-BP03 Perform a thorough analysis of each component](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_thorough_analysis.md): Look at overall cost to the organization of each component.
- [COST05-BP04 Select software with cost-effective licensing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_licensing.md): Open-source software eliminates software licensing costs, which can contribute significant costs to workloads.
- [COST05-BP05 Select components of this workload to optimize cost in line with organization priorities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_select_for_cost.md): Factor in cost when selecting all components for your workload.
- [COST05-BP06 Perform cost analysis for different usage over time](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_select_service_analyze_over_time.md): Workloads can change over time.

### [COST 6. How do you meet cost targets when you select resource type, size and number?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-06.md)

Verify that you choose the appropriate resource size and number of resources for the task at hand.

- [COST06-BP01 Perform cost modeling](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_type_size_number_resources_cost_modeling.md): Identify organization requirements (such as business needs and existing commitments) and perform cost modeling (overall costs) of the workload and each of its components.
- [COST06-BP02 Select resource type, size, and number based on data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_type_size_number_resources_data.md): Select resource size or type based on data about the workload and resource characteristics.
- [COST06-BP03 Select resource type, size, and number automatically based on metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_type_size_number_resources_metrics.md): Use metrics from the currently running workload to select the right size and type to optimize for cost.
- [COST06-BP04 Consider using shared resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_type_size_number_resources_shared.md): For already-deployed services at the organization level for multiple business units, consider using shared resources to increase utilization and reduce total cost of ownership (TCO).

### [COST 7. How do you use pricing models to reduce cost?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-07.md)

Use the pricing model that is most appropriate for your resources to minimize expense.

- [COST07-BP01 Perform pricing model analysis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_pricing_model_analysis.md): Analyze each component of the workload.
- [COST07-BP02 Choose Regions based on cost](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_pricing_model_region_cost.md): Resource pricing may be different in each Region.
- [COST07-BP03 Select third-party agreements with cost-efficient terms](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_pricing_model_third_party.md): Cost efficient agreements and terms ensure the cost of these services scales with the benefits they provide.
- [COST07-BP04 Implement pricing models for all components of this workload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_pricing_model_implement_models.md): Permanently running resources should utilize reserved capacity such as Savings Plans or Reserved Instances.
- [COST07-BP05 Perform pricing model analysis at the management account level](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_pricing_model_master_analysis.md): Check billing and cost management tools and see recommended discounts with commitments and reservations to perform regular analysis at the management account level.

### [COST 8. How do you plan for data transfer charges?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-08.md)

Verify that you plan and monitor data transfer charges so that you can make architectural decisions to minimize costs.

- [COST08-BP01 Perform data transfer modeling](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_data_transfer_modeling.md): Gather organization requirements and perform data transfer modeling of the workload and each of its components.
- [COST08-BP02 Select components to optimize data transfer cost](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_data_transfer_optimized_components.md): All components are selected, and architecture is designed to reduce data transfer costs.
- [COST08-BP03 Implement services to reduce data transfer costs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_data_transfer_implement_services.md): Implement services to reduce data transfer.

### [Manage demand and supply resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-manage-demand-and-supply-resources.md)

Manage demand and supply resources questions and best practices.

### [COST 9. How do you manage demand, and supply resources?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-09.md)

For a workload that has balanced spend and performance, verify that everything you pay for is used and avoid significantly underutilizing instances.

- [COST09-BP01 Perform an analysis on the workload demand](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_manage_demand_resources_cost_analysis.md): Analyze the demand of the workload over time.
- [COST09-BP02 Implement a buffer or throttle to manage demand](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_manage_demand_resources_buffer_throttle.md): Buffering and throttling modify the demand on your workload, smoothing out any peaks.
- [COST09-BP03 Supply resources dynamically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_manage_demand_resources_dynamic.md): Resources are provisioned in a planned manner.

### [Optimize over time](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-optimize-over-time.md)

Optimize over time question and best practices.

### [COST 10. How do you evaluate new services?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-10.md)

As AWS releases new services and features, it's a best practice to review your existing architectural decisions to verify they continue to be the most cost effective.

- [COST10-BP01 Develop a workload review process](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_evaluate_new_services_review_process.md): Develop a process that defines the criteria and process for workload review.
- [COST10-BP02 Review and analyze this workload regularly](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_evaluate_new_services_review_workload.md): Existing workloads are regularly reviewed based on each defined process to find out if new services can be adopted, existing services can be replaced, or workloads can be re-architected.

### [COST 11. How do you evaluate the cost of effort?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost-11.md)

As AWS releases new services and features, it's a best practice to evaluate the cost of the effort it requires to implement new services and features.

- [COST11-BP01 Perform automation for operations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/cost_evaluate_cost_effort_automations_operations.md): Evaluate the operational costs on the cloud, focusing on quantifying the time and effort savings in administrative tasks, deployments, mitigating the risk of human errors, compliance, and other operations through automation.

### [Sustainability](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sustainability.md)

The Sustainability pillar includes understanding the impacts of the services used, quantifying impacts through the entire workload lifecycle, and applying design principles and best practices to reduce these impacts when building cloud workloads.

### [Region selection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-region-selection.md)

Region selection question and best practices

### [SUS 1 How do you select Regions for your workload?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/w2aac19c17b7b5.md)

The choice of Region for your workload significantly affects its KPIs, including performance, cost, and carbon footprint.

- [SUS01-BP01 Choose Region based on both business requirements and sustainability goals](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_region_a2.md): Choose a Region for your workload based on both your business requirements and sustainability goals to optimize its KPIs, including performance, cost, and carbon footprint.

### [Alignment to demand](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-alignment-to-demand.md)

Alignment to demand question and best practices.

### [SUS 2 How do you align cloud resources to your demand?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-02.md)

The way users and applications consume your workloads and other resources can help you identify improvements to meet sustainability goals.

- [SUS02-BP01 Scale workload infrastructure dynamically](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a2.md): Use elasticity of the cloud and scale your infrastructure dynamically to match supply of cloud resources to demand and avoid overprovisioned capacity in your workload.
- [SUS02-BP02 Align SLAs with sustainability goals](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a3.md): Review and optimize workload service-level agreements (SLA) based on your sustainability goals to minimize the resources required to support your workload while continuing to meet business needs.
- [SUS02-BP03 Stop the creation and maintenance of unused assets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a4.md): Decommission unused assets in your workload to reduce the number of cloud resources required to support your demand and minimize waste.
- [SUS02-BP04 Optimize geographic placement of workloads based on their networking requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a5.md): Select cloud location and services for your workload that reduce the distance network traffic must travel and decrease the total network resources required to support your workload.
- [SUS02-BP05 Optimize team member resources for activities performed](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a6.md): Optimize resources provided to team members to minimize the environmental sustainability impact while supporting their needs.
- [SUS02-BP06 Implement buffering or throttling to flatten the demand curve](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_user_a7.md): Buffering and throttling flatten the demand curve and reduce the provisioned capacity required for your workload.

### [Software and architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sus-software-architecture.md)

Software and architecture question and best practices

### [SUS 3 How do you take advantage of software and architecture patterns to support your sustainability goals?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-03.md)

Implement patterns for performing load smoothing and maintaining consistent high utilization of deployed resources to minimize the resources consumed.

- [SUS03-BP01 Optimize software and architecture for asynchronous and scheduled jobs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_software_a2.md): Use efficient software and architecture patterns such as queue-driven to maintain consistent high utilization of deployed resources.
- [SUS03-BP02 Remove or refactor workload components with low or no use](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_software_a3.md): Remove components that are unused and no longer required, and refactor components with little utilization to minimize waste in your workload.
- [SUS03-BP03 Optimize areas of code that consume the most time or resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_software_a4.md): Optimize your code that runs within different components of your architecture to minimize resource usage while maximizing performance.
- [SUS03-BP04 Optimize impact on devices and equipment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_software_a5.md): Understand the devices and equipment used in your architecture and use strategies to reduce their usage.
- [SUS03-BP05 Use software patterns and architectures that best support data access and storage patterns](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_software_a6.md): Understand how data is used within your workload, consumed by your users, transferred, and stored.

### [Data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sus-data.md)

Data question and best practice

### [SUS 4 How do you take advantage of data management policies and patterns to support your sustainability goals?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-04.md)

Implement data management practices to reduce the provisioned storage required to support your workload, and the resources required to use it.

- [SUS04-BP01 Implement a data classification policy](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a2.md): Classify data to understand its criticality to business outcomes and choose the right energy-efficient storage tier to store the data.
- [SUS04-BP02 Use technologies that support data access and storage patterns](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a3.md): Use storage technologies that best support how your data is accessed and stored to minimize the resources provisioned while supporting your workload.
- [SUS04-BP03 Use policies to manage the lifecycle of your datasets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a4.md): Manage the lifecycle of all of your data and automatically enforce deletion to minimize the total storage required for your workload.
- [SUS04-BP04 Use elasticity and automation to expand block storage or file system](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a5.md): Use elasticity and automation to expand block storage or file system as data grows to minimize the total provisioned storage.
- [SUS04-BP05 Remove unneeded or redundant data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a6.md): Remove unneeded or redundant data to minimize the storage resources required to store your datasets.
- [SUS04-BP06 Use shared file systems or storage to access common data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a7.md): Adopt shared file systems or storage to avoid data duplication and allow for more efficient infrastructure for your workload.
- [SUS04-BP07 Minimize data movement across networks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a8.md): Use shared file systems or object storage to access common data and minimize the total networking resources required to support data movement for your workload.
- [SUS04-BP08 Back up data only when difficult to recreate](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_data_a9.md): Avoid backing up data that has no business value to minimize storage resources requirements for your workload.

### [Hardware and services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sus-hardware-and-services.md)

Hardware and services question and best practices.

### [SUS 5 How do you select and use cloud hardware and services in your architecture to support your sustainability goals?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-05.md)

Look for opportunities to reduce workload sustainability impacts by making changes to your hardware management practices.

- [SUS05-BP01 Use the minimum amount of hardware to meet your needs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_hardware_a2.md): Use the minimum amount of hardware for your workload to efficiently meet your business needs.
- [SUS05-BP02 Use instance types with the least impact](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_hardware_a3.md): Continually monitor and use new instance types to take advantage of energy efficiency improvements.
- [SUS05-BP03 Use managed services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_hardware_a4.md): Use managed services to operate more efficiently in the cloud.
- [SUS05-BP04 Optimize your use of hardware-based compute accelerators](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_hardware_a5.md): Optimize your use of accelerated computing instances to reduce the physical infrastructure demands of your workload.

### [Process and culture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/a-sus-process-and-culture.md)

Process and culture process question and best practices

### [SUS 6 How do your organizational processes support your sustainability goals?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus-06.md)

Look for opportunities to reduce your sustainability impact by making changes to your development, test, and deployment practices.

- [SUS06-BP01 Communicate and cascade your sustainability goals](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_dev_a1.md): Technology is a key enabler of sustainability.
- [SUS06-BP02 Adopt methods that can rapidly introduce sustainability improvements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_dev_a2.md): Adopt methods and processes to validate potential improvements, minimize testing costs, and deliver small improvements.
- [SUS06-BP03 Keep your workload up-to-date](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_dev_a3.md): Keep your workload up-to-date to adopt efficient features, remove issues, and improve the overall efficiency of your workload.
- [SUS06-BP04 Increase utilization of build environments](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_dev_a4.md): Increase the utilization of resources to develop, test, and build your workloads.
- [SUS06-BP05 Use managed device farms for testing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/sus_sus_dev_a5.md): Use managed device farms to efficiently test a new feature on a representative set of hardware.


